'' A CONVERSION CONSTRUCTOR WITH A DEFAULTED TAIL converts like an arity-1 one: 'constructor(
'' byref a as const DT, byval b as long = 7, byref t as const string = "dflt" )' given a DT,
'' into an overload set (both declaration orders), byval, 'byref const', a function argument
'' and 'dim as LDay q = t'. fbc-modern 1.20 prints exactly these lines (measured 2026-11-23).
'' tiko costed only arity-1 constructors: P1 / Q1 silently called the 'long' overload, P2 / P3
'' were TKO0698, and once accepted the byval path blitted the DT's bytes with no constructor.
'' Tko.Check.StructorTakesOne (structpick.tiko), used by UserConvCost_, StructorUserConvCost
'' and lowering's HasUdtConvCtor_ / DirectUdtCtor_ / ConvCtorFor_.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/udt-ctor-default-tail-arg.bas -o tests/codegen/udtctordefaulttailarg.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/udtctordefaulttailarg.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/udtctordefaulttailarg.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: P1 LDay  12 dflt
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Q1 LDay  12 dflt
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: P2  12 dflt
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: P3  12 dflt
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: P4  24
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dim  12 dflt
